From: RitzDaCat <49771174+RitzDaCat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 13:40:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] latency: correlate complete frames and cold color state

Capture every completed frame only while the bounded exact-kernel mode is active.
Add phase timestamps around pre-paint, layer selection, direct-scanout
preparation, rendering, post-paint, presentation queueing, DRM queueing,
atomic submission, pageflip, and callback delivery. Flush in per-output
bounded batches after timestamps have been recorded so global frame numbering
cannot strand one monitor's telemetry tail.

Log the requested color pipeline, hardware assignment, compensation
decisions, and cold-path matching wall-clock time.
The normal policy continues to execute only capture-disabled branches and
performs no clock reads, file writes, allocations, or logging.
